# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Group type — broadcast method calls to all members in parallel;
#         Group.new() << member chaining; assignment broadcasts to all members.
# defer-to: M6 (requires Group stdlib type and class/method dispatch)
#
# Reason:
#   The Group type is a stdlib concurrency helper scheduled for M6.  It depends
#   on prototype-OOP method dispatch (M4) for member method invocation and on
#   ',' parallel invocation semantics (M5) to broadcast calls concurrently.
#   Class definition with 'class C { var val = 0 }' also requires M4.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Group type and full stdlib):
# # class C { var val = 0 }|; var a = C.new()|; var b = C.new()|;
# # var g2 = Group.new() << a << b|;
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/groups.chk)
